## How to Add a New Page/View

1. Create `src/components/MyView.tsx`
2. Add routing logic in `src/App.tsx` (currently uses conditional rendering based on auth state — extend with your own view state or add a router like `react-router-dom`)
3. Use existing UI primitives from `src/components/ui/` (Button, Card, Input, Dialog, etc.)

---

## How to Extend the Zustand Store

In `src/store/appStore.ts`:

```typescript
interface AppState {
  // Add your state fields
  myData: MyType | null;
  setMyData: (data: MyType) => void;
}

export const useAppStore = create<AppState>((set) => ({
  // Add defaults + setters
  myData: null,
  setMyData: (myData) => set({ myData }),
}));
```

Use in components: `const { myData, setMyData } = useAppStore();`

---

## How to Add a New Error Type

In `src-tauri/src/error.rs`, add a variant to `AppError`:

```rust
#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
pub enum AppError {
    #[error("My custom error: {0}")]
    MyError(String),
    // ... existing variants
}
```

All `AppError` variants are serialized as strings via the `Serialize` impl and sent to the frontend as error messages.

---

## How to Add Shared App State

In `src-tauri/src/state.rs`, add fields to `AppState`:

```rust
pub struct AppState {
    pub my_cache: HashMap<String, String>,
    // ... existing fields
}
```

Access in commands via `State<'_, SharedState>` (which is `Mutex<AppState>`).

---

## How to Add Persistent Settings

1. **Rust model** — add field to `src-tauri/src/models/settings.rs`:
   ```rust
   pub struct AppSettings {
       pub my_setting: Option<String>,
       // ... existing fields
   }
   ```

2. **TypeScript mirror** — add field to `src/lib/types.ts`:
   ```typescript
   export interface AppSettings {
     mySetting: string | null;
     // ... existing fields
   }
   ```

Settings are persisted via `tauri-plugin-store` to a JSON file on disk. The `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]` attribute handles `snake_case` ↔ `camelCase` conversion automatically.

---

## How to Add a Tauri Plugin

1. Add the plugin crate to `src-tauri/Cargo.toml`:
   ```toml
   tauri-plugin-myplugin = "2"
   ```

2. Register in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`:
   ```rust
   .plugin(tauri_plugin_myplugin::init())
   ```

3. Grant permissions in `src-tauri/capabilities/default.json`:
   ```json
   "permissions": ["myplugin:default"]
   ```

4. Install the JS binding (if the plugin has one):
   ```bash
   bun add @tauri-apps/plugin-myplugin
   ```

