## Common Patterns

### Calling Rust from React
```typescript
import * as api from "@/lib/tauri";
try {
  const result = await api.myCommand(arg);
} catch (error) {
  // error is the serialized AppError string
  console.error(error);
}
```

### Using the settings hook
```typescript
const { settings, updateSettings, pickFolder } = useSettings();
await updateSettings({ theme: "dark" });
const folder = await pickFolder();
```

### Opening external URLs
```typescript
import { openUrl } from "@tauri-apps/plugin-opener";
await openUrl("https://example.com");
```

### Persistent storage (Rust side)
```rust
use tauri_plugin_store::StoreExt;
let store = app.store("mydata.json").map_err(|e| AppError::Other(e.to_string()))?;
store.set("key", serde_json::json!("value"));
let val = store.get("key");
```
